  "slug": "cortex-visual-b857",
  "summary": "Three September 2026 preprints pair video-model features with human visual cortex fMRI, adding routing, receptive-field, and generative-alignment analyses.",
  "synthesis": "The three preprints share a focus on predicting human visual cortex fMRI responses from video-trained or video-generative representations. The first routes V-JEPA-2 video features across space and time through a cross-attention encoding model, targeting higher visual cortex and dynamic spatiotemporal structure. The second introduces RF-DiVE and RF-GO, population receptive field-constrained most-exciting-input frameworks for encoding models spanning V1 through hV4, with in-silico validation. The third reports that representations from future-frame generation in video diffusion models align better with fMRI responses than representations of observed video. Together they extend encoding-model work toward temporally resolved, receptive-field-aware, and generative representational spaces. The common thread is the use of video models as probes of cortical visual representation; the receptive-field and generative-alignment findings are the novel elements, with the scope of each limited to the reported in-silico and fMRI settings.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-01"
}
